### Topic 59 - Microservices intro
### Start product-service (8081) and order-service (8082) first.
### VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request" above each request.

### 1. product-service directly: all products
GET http://localhost:8081/api/products

### 2. product-service directly: one product
GET http://localhost:8081/api/products/1

### 3. product-service: unknown product -> 404
GET http://localhost:8081/api/products/99

### 4. order-service: place an order (order-service calls product-service for you)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 2
}

### 5. order-service: order for an unknown product -> 404 (passed on from product-service)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 99,
  "quantity": 1
}

### 6. order-service: too many items -> 409 Conflict
POST http://localhost:8082/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 500
}

### 7. order-service: list orders
GET http://localhost:8082/api/orders

### 8. Health checks
GET http://localhost:8081/actuator/health

###
GET http://localhost:8082/actuator/health

### 9. EXPERIMENT: stop product-service (Ctrl+C), then send request 4 again -> 503
